  "articleBody": "Deciding to install a walk-in tub is a big step towards enhancing bathroom accessibility and safety. While some might consider a DIY approach, there are clear signs that bringing in a professional is not just helpful, but necessary. For starters, if the installation involves any plumbing or electrical work, or if permits are required by your local authorities in areas like Denver, Centennial, or Highlands Ranch, it's definitely time to call in the experts. Professionals know the codes and can ensure everything is up to standard. Another key indicator is if your bathroom needs significant rerouting of pipes or even structural repair to accommodate the new tub. This isn't just about dropping a tub in place; it's about ensuring the underlying structure can handle the weight and demands. Moreover, if your project requires coordinating multiple trades—like a plumber, an electrician, and a carpenter—a general contractor can manage all those moving parts efficiently, ensuring compliance and a smooth process. HH Remodeling LLC specializes in these kinds of comprehensive projects, making sure all the complex details are handled correctly and efficiently.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}